00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
welcome back to new rockstars i'm eric  voss and this is a no spoiler review of  doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness i was lucky this time to get  invited to the film's la premiere last  night i learned my eyes and skin do not  comply with natural light outside of the  blue dungeon and i spent the screening  scribbling so many notes for the  breakdown that my thumb is still blue  with ink so as i walked out of the  theater i was still processing and  couldn't really put my thoughts into  words now we do not normally review  movies here on new rockstars honestly  because i think most people don't need  my advice on whether or not to see a  movie and i think there are just so many  more interesting things to say about a  film beyond a numerical score but with  all the interesting hot takes coming  about this film i think it helps to go  into it with a healthy mindset now again  no spoilers in this review and my  friends tread carefully down there in  the comments and on social media until  you see the movie so some general  thoughts doctor strange in the  multiverse madness delivers on the  promise of the mcu's first true horror  film with director sam raimi bleeding  his signature horror into every frame it  is the mcu's most violent film by a long  shot the body count is high and you feel  every fatality which is something i have  always felt the mcu could use some more  of but the squeamish among you can relax  while raymie has earned his reputation  as a master of horror cinema his  approach to the genre always comes with  a smirk whether it's the violent  delights of bruce campbell's ash in the  evil dead series the shot and freud of  wanting the damn didn't drag me to hell  to get dragged to hell or even the  sudden jump scares in his spider-man  films the mcu is after all live-action  toys smacking into each other and it's  okay for them to have to spit out some  blood every now and then multiverse of  madness's strengths come from the extent  to which they allow sam raimi to  actually evolve the aesthetics rainey  and his cinematographer john matheson  let the camera glide bend distort and  superimpose in ways you have never seen  after the marvel studios fanfare evoking  something closer to the surrealist  montages of rosemary's baby danny  elfman's score surrounds us and binds us  with madcap evil that said the film also  totally works as a marvel studios even  whatever you may have seen or theorized  or speculated over the marvel tie-ins  and surprises will have you pinching  yourself and screaming yes while the  nerd sitting next to you scribbling a  notepad tells you to shut up personally  i was equally thrilled with the theories  we got right as i was with the stuff  that went in a very different direction  marvel's producers proved once again  that they have a more nuanced approach  to how far to go with the fan service  hats off to that forever hatted mr feige  screenwriter michael waldron brought his  multiverse world building expertise from  loki on disney plus as well as on rick  and morty and on every level he hides  subtle winks that make the future of the  mcu multiverse as bright as it is brutal  the script also widens the mcu lexicon  with a glossary of terms and dream  redefining concepts that for me have  always been the most crucial  contribution of doctor strange to this  whole universe the rules are set up in  the first act and then in the climax  flourish with demonic delight like all  mcu films at this point multiverse of  madness certainly rewards having done  the homework if you have time maybe  review one division in the 2016 doctor  strange film as well as the animated  what if series and to my surprise  avengers infinity war in fact without  going into more detail i would say  infinity war might be the most important  mcu film to watch before this movie but  this is all truly the climax who won  division most of us went into one of  vision framing it as a prelude series  for multiverse madness and despite  doctor strange saying in trailers that  he's not here to talk about west view  this movie is very much about what went  down in west view and it is at its  creepiest and most heartbreaking when it  dives back into that hex which brings me  to what i wanted to see more of in this  movie oh my god new rockstar stinks an  mcu movie wasn't perfect cancel this man  now breaking these things down is the  skill that the gods have called me to do  but do you have a specific skill that  you are trying to learn maybe it's even  one that could help your career like  graphic design or learning how to write  a business plan well skillshare the  sponsor of this video can help you  invest in yourself and your personal  growth in 2022. skillshare is an online  learning community with thousands of  inspiring classes for anyone who loves  learning and wants to explore their  creativity and learn new skills from  photography and illustration to  gardening freelancing and more you can  find classes that will match your goals  and interests they've got a deep roster  of classes on animation design and  photography so you can transition from  just enjoying other people's content to  making your own skillshare is ad-free  and new premium classes are launched  each week the entire catalog is now  available with subtitles in spanish  french portuguese and german the first 1  000 of my subscribers to click the link  in the description or use my code new  rockstars will get a one month free  trial of skillshare so you can start  exploring your creativity today now on  to some stuff that i wish we saw more of  dr strange's multiverse behind us maybe  it's the place wand division now  occupies in our hearts but dr strange  and the multiverse madness might have  been better framed as the scarlet witch  in the multiverse of madness because  elizabeth olsen's wanda maximoff is the  broken heart driving this film and as we  do with mia farrow and rosemary's baby  or even elphaba and wicked i connected  far more with her than i did with dr  strange's relationship with christine  palmer or with his variants or with  america chavez i cannot wait to see  zochi gomez more in the mcu especially  when she's out from under strange's wing  but as written in this story the  character often comes off as more of a  plot function than a patient the msu's  chief surgeon feels an emotional drive  to save maybe it's just the next day and  i'm still overwhelmed by all the other  masters this movie serves maybe i'll  feel differently when i rewatch it but  at this moment i just feel like i never  wondered what the emotional stakes for  strange were in the 2016 film or even in  the best episode from what if episode 4  but in this movie things did feel at  times a bit disjointed with any movie we  always ask ourselves what is the core  dramatic relationship of this film in  this case is it about strange and  christine is it about strange in america  is it about strange in wanda is it about  strange in his other stranges strange in  the multiverse at different parts of the  movie the answer to the question changes  you may also see some griping about the  way this story treats wanda as a  cold-hearted villain arguably unaffected  by her experiences with vision and  wanavision but i would say wandavision's  post-credits scene already made that  sudden dark turn every mcu title has to  choose which parts of a character's  backstory to suddenly make important for  them in the next chapter and i just  can't wait to see the flashback scene in  the title i gag at the house of  heartness showing the heartbreaking  chapter in which wanda alone in her  cabin suddenly decides like all humans  sometimes do that our own needs  supersede everything else in our world  folks this whole mcu love it or hate it  is characterization across titles and  across media distribution formats and if  we can forgive tony stark for in the  same movie going from feeling so much  guilt over getting a kid killed to  binding his whole team to legislative  oversight who in the second act  endangering the child ultimate civil war  cooler we could certainly forgive wanda  for not embracing the quote what is  grief if not love persevering as her  mantra as much as we inked it as our  pandemic tattoos and now equally worthy  of our consideration is this film's  questions like how do we fill the holes  in our hearts is happiness truly the  highest pursuit now with everything in  this movie your mileage may vary which  is also the case when it comes to  whether multiverse madness is too  intense for you i will say that it is  safely pg-13 and no more violent than  episodes of what if were i mean that  show did repeatedly slaughter tony stark  and popped hulk  so you do you my final thoughts  multiverse of madness was not the film i  expected and i love it for that i was  shocked at how much marvel studios would  unleash sam raimi to wreak his madness  on the mcu toy box it is a bold vicious  thriller with images that will haunt me  forever no numerical score from me i'm  sorry it's just too early for me to  cement this movie's legacy just to give  haters or stands ammo to scream at each  other there's plenty of other real movie  critics for that i hope you enjoyed dr  strange's multiverse madness as much as  i did and once you see it send me your  thoughts follow me on twitter and  instagram at eavos following a rockstar  subscribing rockstar some more analysis  of everything you love thanks for  watching bye  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

